  partName: Exhaust Manifold Stud (2)
  description: The Exhaust Manifold Stud (2) is a tiny, elongated stud located at
    the middle-left-front of the engine, serving as a threaded fastener for the exhaust
    manifold. Its primary purpose is to provide a secure mounting point for the exhaust
    manifold, enabling efficient exhaust gas flow and reducing the risk of leaks.
    Interestingly, the stud's material, Material.001, is chosen for its high strength-to-weight
    ratio, allowing it to withstand extreme temperatures and pressures.
